.TH WPS-SESSION 1 "@DATE@" "WPS @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wps-session \- the WPS session, from the login screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wps-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wps-session
is what
.B WPS
on the login screen starts: wps-compositor on the screens and input
devices, the WPS desktop in it, and wpsd. GNOME's settings (keyboard
layouts, input methods, the pointer, light or dark) are shared with the
GNOME session.
.PP
It needs a real seat (a console, or a virtual machine's screen); it does
not run over remote desktop logins. Never start it inside another running
session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/wps/session.log
The session's log (the one before:
.IR session.log.old ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/wps/session.env
Settings for the session, one
.IB NAME = value
a line (for example
.B WLR_RENDERER=pixman
to draw in software).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wps-shell (1),
.BR wpsctl (1)
